  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Protection of Vulnerable Host Communities in Cox&apos;s Bazar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vulnerable populations are at an increased risk of trafficking in persons and gender-based violence (GBV) because of limited awareness and knowledge of indicators and risks within their community. Building on the International Organization for Migration (IOM)&apos;s operational capacity as one of the largest humanitarian agencies in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, this project seeks to utilize the Organization&apos;s ability to access at-risk communities to implement proactive prevention measures through awareness raising activities targeting individuals across multiple locations. It aims to fill protection gaps for GBV survivors, victims of trafficking (VoTs) and at-risk populations based on identified challenges, continual assessment of existing protection needs and capacity of service providers. This is further supported through the provision culturally appropriate and sensitive information about risks and referral advice. Through direct community engagement, the project envisions to better equip IOM staff and implementing partner, Bangladesh National Woman Lawyers&apos; Association (BNWLA), to identify VoTs and provide specialized support. In this pursuit, BNWLA&#x2019;s extensive counter-trafficking knowledge working with the host community will help to reach more VoTs and at-risk populations.</narrative>
  </description>
